edge they meet. The bounds"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are upper bounds only. Positions are never reused, so a bound counts every position ever handed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"out, and nothing in the library allocates by it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"In addition to ","type":"text"},{"code":"Graph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s laws:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"containsVertex(atPosition: p)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is true exactly for the positions of live vertices, all in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"0..<vertexPositionBound","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertexPosition(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertex(atPosition:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" are inverses, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" lists the live vertices in increasing position. Likewise","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"containsEdge(atPosition:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is true exactly for the positions in ","type":"text"},{"code":"edges","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", all in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"0..<edgePositionBound","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which ","type":"text"},{"code":"edges","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" lists in increasing order.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Without holes, the bounds equal ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertexIndexBound","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"edgeIndexBound","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and positions are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"indices.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_numberedIncidenceRows()"},{"type":"text","text":" numbers the live ve